WEBVTT

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:10.780
I see. So that's what happened.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:16.000
You've been through a lot to get here.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:18.250
You're incredible.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:23.090
No, I'm not. Not at all.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.710
I couldn't save them.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:28.720
Guy.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:32.550
Vilma.

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.230
It's not your fault.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:41.850
That Mr. Fancy Pants.
I can't believe he did that for us.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:43.690
Vilma, too.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:46.940
She was such a great gal.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.990
Please let me through.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.280
I have to take Arlequin to Shirogane.

00:00:56.830 --> 00:01:02.170
Sorry, but I'd rather you not bother her
until it's really necessary.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:18.640
Am I destined to lose my way?

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:21.810
All I want is to have fun in my life

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:28.030
All I want is to be with those I love

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:34.280
Ready or not
Here I come

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:37.160
I don't care anymore

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.950
I just don't know anymore

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:43.500
I wish everything would just disappear

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.630
There are days when I think like that

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:49.550
But everything is precious to me

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:52.380
And so I fight on

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:55.890
Today was a tough day

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.970
I almost gave up hope

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:05.020
But the truth is I don't want
to lose anything anymore

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.690
I wish everything would just disappear

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:11.940
There are days when I think like that

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:14.700
But everything is precious to me

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:17.740
And so I must fight

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.300
#32 Valediction

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:36.590
Why? What do you mean?

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:40.390
When you two joined Nakamachi Circus,

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.230
you brought a smile back to our
gloomy little group.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.770
We're really grateful to you, Masaru.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:50.570
And to Shirogane, too.

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:57.030
So we want to give Shirogane
something she hasn't had for 90 years.

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:03.040
To tell you the truth, we saw it all.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.580
All of Shirogane's memories.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.920
Her memories?

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:12.300
Yeah, the situation called for it.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.520
Oh no...

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:30.520
How awful...

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:35.440
Until she met you,

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:39.450
all her memories were of
how much of her blood was spilled.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:49.290
She never played house
like any other child.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:53.750
Nor dressed herself up
like any other teenager.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:58.510
She just fought automata, all on her own,

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:01.800
while living as a circus entertainer.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.890
She believed that was her duty.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:08.770
What human lives like that?

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:14.570
But then.

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:21.910
Around the time you and that man
entered her life.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.870
Shirogane's memories,

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.870
they start to become colorful.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.010
Can you believe it?

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:42.180
For 90 years, she was just an instrument,
fighting longer than any soldier.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:46.020
But then came her memories
of a single man.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:52.190
A man she was with for only a day.
She's replayed it thousands of times.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:03.240
And they must be pretty precious memories.

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:06.450
They sparkle like none of her
other memories.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.210
What else could we do once we'd seen that?

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.290
We want to make her happy.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:19.470
The man Shirogane loves will be sent up
to Faceless's space station.

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:22.840
To ask him how to stop ZONAPHA.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:27.640
And he won't be coming back.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:32.270
So this is for Shirogane.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:35.610
So she can spend as much time
as she can with him.

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.860
That's why we protect this train.

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:41.780
You mean...

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:46.280
Narumi is here...?

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.790
Yeah, he's in the first car.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:54.460
But he won't be coming back?

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:57.040
No.

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:01.550
Narumi!

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:03.470
-Wait!
-Stop!

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:06.010
Narumi!

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:11.390
Behind that door is...

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:15.650
the man that taught me strength.

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.400
The man I thought had died to save me.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.280
I missed him.

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:27.370
I missed him so much.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.290
Narumi!

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:41.170
What...?

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:43.300
Move.

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.220
I'm going to meet Narumi.

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:47.760
Move!

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:53.680
We act only for the utmost happiness
of Lady Francine.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:59.820
If you believe that going in
to meet Narumi is what's best for her,

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:00.730
you may pass.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.700
Shirogane's happiness...

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.250
That's right.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:20.090
Shirogane probably...

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:22.460
loves Narumi.

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:29.140
And they've finally reunited.

00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:32.560
We saw it all.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:35.560
All of Shirogane's memories.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:40.230
What else could we do once we'd seen that?

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:42.980
We want to make her happy.

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:01.840
I'm sorry.

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:06.800
I'd only been thinking about myself.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:12.180
Me going in there...

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:18.270
isn't what's best
for Shirogane's happiness.

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:26.400
We're sorry, Masaru.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:30.530
Come on. Let's talk in the back car.

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:36.910
We're now on the Trans-Siberian Railway.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:41.330
We will reach the Bodny launch site
in about 60 hours.

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:50.050
60 hours? That's fast.

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:53.350
Yes, usually it'd take 5 days.

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:57.310
But Mr. Fou modified the suspension
and fitted up a special system.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:00.230
This train can go 130 km an hour
on average, so...

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:01.520
Keep away from me!

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:04.440
I'm sorry.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:09.820
So, what about the engine?

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:15.580
The memories of experienced engineers were
downloaded into Mr. Fou's maid automata.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:17.750
They control the system.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:23.960
To maintain top speed, they stoke
the engine according to the topography

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:28.840
and continuously monitor and adjust
the wheels and suspension.

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:31.340
There are 6 backup maid puppets, too.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:33.840
The train won't stop, no matter what.

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:36.310
Fou's maid puppets, you say?

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:41.140
You're saying this train is being run
by those blasted automata?

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:42.230
Well, yes...

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:44.350
Over my dead body!

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:47.020
But we've already come this far...

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:52.990
That old infernal Fou.
Making a fool out of me.

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:01.120
Masaru's fallen asleep.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.000
He bore it well.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:07.460
Don't wake him. Eat up while you can.

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:16.800
This pre-packed preserved food...

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.140
Tastes like crap.

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:23.310
I'd make something for you
if only there were a kitchen.

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:26.150
I was talking to myself.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:28.270
Not to you.

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:30.280
I'm sorry.

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:34.990
Well.

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:39.080
Your casserole was a lot better than this.

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:48.170
Narumi?

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:50.250
You...

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:53.300
Your memory has come back?

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:01.060
The casserole...

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:06.310
That's what I made when we first met.

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:10.820
So?

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:13.570
What about it?

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:19.410
I also heard from Fou,
who saw your memories.

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:23.830
That you have nothing to do
with Doll Francine.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.630
But still.

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:33.210
Does that change this situation?

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:37.380
The children.

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:41.350
The people, all around the world.
Will that cure them?

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:47.980
Say I remembered everything
and you become happy again.

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:50.020
So what?

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:55.360
Once we reach that launch pad,
I'm going up into space.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:12:00.620
To make Faceless spill his guts
about how to stop ZONAPHA.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:02.700
And...

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:05.620
I won't be coming back.

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:11.880
What could you want from me?

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:17.880
A memory? Those only make you sad.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:32.020
Here it comes. There it is.

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:37.280
Our captain knows everything.
You can really count on him.

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:43.330
That fool, losing 3,000 automata
to a human's simple trap.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:49.790
But thanks to that, we get to
mess with that train all by ourselves.

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:51.380
I agree.

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:56.090
I hear Arlequino and the man named Kato
are on that train.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:13:00.430
Jeez, all you think about is fighting.

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:03.890
By the way, where's Diamantina?

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:08.390
Who knows? She's been strange
ever since she fought Colombine.

00:13:08.770 --> 00:13:12.940
Oh well. Lord Faceless isn't here.

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:15.940
-So let's enjoy our free time...
-Let's go.

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:16.860
Huh?

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:22.820
Hey, wake up Masaru.

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:27.620
Get up.

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:40.220
Finally, I've caught up with you.

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:43.510
I haven't had such a nice Sunday
in a long time.

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:46.010
Mom!

00:13:49.810 --> 00:13:51.640
F-Fusae...!

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:54.060
What do you mean?

00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:58.190
Don't ask me.
Why does that monster have Mom's face?

00:13:58.530 --> 00:14:02.280
That's not Fusae. Fusae is dead!

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:07.780
I'm going with Mom!

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:10.290
The circus...

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:12.870
must never...

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:15.920
stop the show...

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:18.880
Mom!

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:20.630
Mom...

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:24.890
"Mom," huh?

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:28.970
When I come back...

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:32.980
maybe I really will become your Mom.

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:39.570
Unforgivable.

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:42.690
A monster, looking just like Fusae...!

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:45.530
We three will take it on.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:47.450
Masaru, you stay back.

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:51.080
-No, I'm going too. There's another one.
-What?

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:57.330
I know him. He's really strong.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:00.590
Give that case to Shirogane.

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:04.930
Damn it, I'm going to kill it.

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:08.260
Yeah, that creepy monster with Mom's face.

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:12.640
Stay calm. We only have one knife each
from Vilma and that's it.

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:16.850
We don't know how to use
Fou's special weapons.

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:20.770
We probably don't have
the slightest chance of winning.

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:24.110
But Fou told me something before we left.

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:31.030
We shiroganes always learn
how to do circus tricks first.

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:32.740
Why's that?

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:40.250
It has to do with long ago
when automata were first created.

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:47.130
They were originally made
to make Doll Francine laugh.

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:52.930
Silly movements and funny tricks.

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:56.270
They're all instilled in their bodies.

00:15:56.890 --> 00:16:00.940
It's their duty to think up new tricks.

00:16:02.820 --> 00:16:03.780
So...?

00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:10.530
So when they meet
human performers without any weapons...

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:12.910
What happens then?

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:19.670
They subconsciously try to learn
the performers' tricks.

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:26.420
They focus on the performance,
hoping to glean a new trick.

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:30.260
It's pretty much an instinct.

00:16:30.430 --> 00:16:32.800
They can't help themselves.

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:38.390
It wouldn't take a shirogane
to kill them then, you see?

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:41.480
Nakamachi Circus.

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:44.650
So if we are true performers...

00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:49.740
True circus performers...

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:52.950
We might be able to defeat them.

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:56.160
They've caught up.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:59.660
Yes, I see it's time.

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:02.500
You sense it too?

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:07.630
Two automata.
Probably Brighella and Harlequin.

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:10.430
Then let us go take our leave.

00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:20.850
What?

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:23.190
Excuse us.

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:32.450
What do you want?

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:37.290
Forgive us for intruding upon you.

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:41.750
The enemy is closing in,
and we must go to intercept them.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:46.040
So we have come
to request your permission.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:48.090
To leave your side for a while.

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:49.710
-The enemy?
-How many?

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:52.340
They are still far away.

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:56.470
But they will stop this train
if allowed to continue.

00:17:56.970 --> 00:18:01.060
Only we puppets can sense them.

00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:02.600
Okay, I'm going.

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:07.690
Have you forgotten your mission?
Do not be so foolish.

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:10.740
How can I trust you?

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.780
Narumi, you are strong.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:17.990
I know, as I have fought you.

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:23.710
Once we are gone, you are the only one
to whom we can entrust Lady Éléonore.

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:27.790
Gone? You mean...

00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:33.970
Now, if you will excuse us.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:36.720
Wait.

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:45.060
I used to think that you were the enemy.

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:47.810
You are not to be blamed.

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:51.070
But you're going off to fight for me.

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:54.400
For humankind.

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:58.070
And I don't know anymore.

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:02.830
I have fought against you for 90 years.

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:06.620
I don't know what to say to you now.

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.880
It is simple, my lady.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:16.180
We exist for you and for nothing else.

00:19:16.680 --> 00:19:18.970
So here is what you say.

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:22.220
"Fight."

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:24.730
"And win."

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:35.200
Then I order you to fight and to win.

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:39.200
And to come back alive.

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:50.750
Lady Francine has given us an order!

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:53.920
She has finally told us to fight.

00:19:58.970 --> 00:20:00.300
Will I see it again?

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:04.310
That smile that gave me
a strange sensation.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:05.810
Whatever is that?

00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:08.560
The smile of a human girl.

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:14.940
It shone like a star sparkling on
the surface of a quietly rippling lake.

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:21.830
Well, I'm interested in the circus
that Lady Francine was in.

00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:25.830
I wish to mime and sing with them.

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:29.580
I can sing too, you know.

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:31.880
Well then.

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:33.630
If you can sing,

00:20:35.340 --> 00:20:38.010
sing for me some time.

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:41.760
Sure, under a circus tent one day.

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:47.770
Lady Spider, you have brought me here
in comfort.

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:52.020
Now I shall bravely stop that train
by myself.

00:20:56.940 --> 00:21:00.990
Masaru Saiga, I see you wish to duel.

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:03.910
I like your resolution.

00:21:05.790 --> 00:21:11.210
I care not why you're not up in space
as a vessel for Lord Faceless's mind.

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:14.630
You are the enemy for guarding the train.
I will defeat you!

00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:19.590
Bow to my blade of destruction,
"Spezza Ferro"!

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:24.930
I will drink up all of your blood.

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:32.060
So, you are my dinner tonight.

00:21:32.230 --> 00:21:34.650
What a delightful Sunday.

00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:42.950
Oh dear, my husband and my sons.

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:46.950
Why do you run so? This is no fun.

00:21:48.750 --> 00:21:49.910
Let's do it, Pops.

00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:53.290
I can't stand this monster
that has Mom's face.

00:21:53.880 --> 00:21:56.710
All right, boys. Don't mess this up!

00:21:56.880 --> 00:21:58.670
We got it, Pops.

00:21:58.880 --> 00:22:00.800
All or nothing, here we go!

00:22:20.780 --> 00:22:25.240
A past that can't become a memory
plays on repeat

00:22:25.450 --> 00:22:30.160
In my mind is a forgotten thing
that I still remember

00:22:30.330 --> 00:22:34.830
Questions remain unanswered
but I must go now

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:39.710
I walk in the dark,
making a promise to my footprints

00:22:39.880 --> 00:22:44.380
So many similar beings
leading similar lives

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:49.100
Was there a reason
for me to be born at all?

00:22:49.260 --> 00:22:53.850
The world lost all sound
but for the ticking of a clock

00:22:54.020 --> 00:22:58.690
A missing heart keeps shouting

00:22:58.860 --> 00:23:03.490
A meaningless life was shaking

00:23:03.650 --> 00:23:08.200
All because of your unique existence

00:23:08.370 --> 00:23:12.830
If the reason for the pain
is revealed someday

00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:17.580
If you find a home
for those tears someday

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:22.670
You shall sleep
with the whole universe in your arms

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:30.560
I know it still plays in your heart

00:23:30.890 --> 00:23:34.560
The melody that brought you here
